                     aria-controls="faq1">
                     What is white label accounting? 
 
                  </h5>
                  <div id="faq1"
                     class="accordion-collapse collapse show"
                     data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                     <p>
                        White label accounting is a service model in which accounting work is done by an outside team but delivered under your firm's brand. Your clients deal with you and see your name, while the outsourcing team handles the work quietly in the background.

                     </p>
                  </div>
               </div>
               <!-- FAQ 2 -->
               <div class="fre_que">
                  <h5 class="sub_head collapsed"
                     data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                     data-bs-target="#faq2"
                     aria-expanded="false"
                     aria-controls="faq2">
                    How is white label accounting different from outsourcing? 
                  </h5>
                  <div id="faq2"
                     class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                     data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                     <p>
                    With normal outsourcing, the other firm is often visible to your client. White label is invisible. We never appear to your clients, so your brand stays at the centre throughout.
                     </p>
                  </div>
               </div>
               <!-- FAQ 3 -->
